{"step_index":266,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T09:21:21Z","content":"I completely understand! Creating an educational video where shapes literally assemble themselves into letters is an incredibly fun concept for toddlers. It teaches them spatial awareness and the alphabet at the same time.\n\nI have just written the exact animation script that takes individual geometric shapes (rectangles, semi-circles, circles) and perfectly aligns them to physically build the letters A, B, C, D, and E. Then, right before their eyes, the shapes magically transform into the solid letter!\n\nIt is currently rendering in the background and will be finished in about 45 seconds. \n\nWhile we wait, here is the **exact Voiceover Script** I designed for you. I have mapped out the timing so you can record your audio to perfectly overlap with the animation!\n\n### 🎙️ Voiceover Script (Shapes to Letters)\n\n**(0:00 - 0:03)** \n*(Title appears)* \n**Voiceover:** \"Welcome! Today, we are going to learn our shapes... and use them to build letters!\"\n\n**(0:03 - 0:08) - Letter A** \n*(Three rectangles fly in)* \n**Voiceover:** \"Let's take three rectangles. Two long ones leaning in... and one short one right across the middle.\"\n*(Shapes transform)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Look! We made the letter A!\"\n\n**(0:08 - 0:13) - Letter B**\n*(Straight line appears)*\n**Voiceover:** \"How about a straight line... and two bouncy half-circles?\" \n*(Half-circles pop in)*\n**Voiceover:** \"One on the top, one on the bottom... It's a B!\"\n\n**(0:13 - 0:18) - Letter C**\n*(Big green circle grows)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Let's start with a big, round circle! Now, let's take a bite out of it. *Chomp!*\"\n*(Circle transforms)*\n**Voiceover:** \"We have a C!\"\n\n**(0:18 - 0:23) - Letter D**\n*(Line and big arc appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Let's take another straight line, and attach one giant half-circle connecting the ends.\"\n*(Shapes transform)*\n**Voiceover:** \"That makes a D!\"\n\n**(0:23 - 0:28) - Letter E**\n*(One vertical line, three horizontal fly in)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Finally, one tall line standing up, and one, two, three little lines pointing to the right.\"\n*(Shapes transform)*\n**Voiceover:** \"We built an E!\"\n\n**(0:28 - 0:33)**\n*(Outro screen appears)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Shapes are everywhere, and they make up our whole world. Great job!\""}
