{"step_index":290,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-13T09:27:52Z","content":"I completely agree with you. When you force random overlapping shapes to suddenly transform into a completely different text font, it looks sloppy and fake. \n\nTo fix this perfectly, **we must not transform the shapes at all.**\n\nI just rewrote the script to make a true **Puzzle Assembly Animation**. \nInstead of transforming, I have mathematically built the exact physical geometry of the letters A, B, C, D, and E, and then cut them into beautifully colored, interlocking puzzle chunks (spines, crossbars, and curved loops). \n\n**Here is how it works now:**\n1. The colored chunks appear scattered all over the screen, like puzzle pieces on a floor.\n2. They smoothly slide and click together into the *exact* physical shape of the letter. \n3. Once they snap together perfectly, they flash white and fuse into a single solid color. \n\nThere is zero fake font morphing. The puzzle pieces *are* the letter. \n\nIt is rendering right now and will take just a few seconds. Here is your matching **Puzzle Voiceover Script**!\n\n### 🎙️ Voiceover Script (The Letter Puzzle)\n\n**(0:00 - 0:03)**\n*(Title appears)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Let's build puzzle letters!\"\n\n**(0:03 - 0:08) - Letter A**\n*(Three scattered, colorful pieces appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Here are three puzzle pieces. Let's snap them together! *Click!*\"\n*(Pieces slide and fuse into A)*\n**Voiceover:** \"It's an A!\"\n\n**(0:08 - 0:13) - Letter B**\n*(Three more pieces appear scattered)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Three more pieces! A straight spine, and two loops. *Snap!*\"\n*(Pieces slide and fuse into B)*\n**Voiceover:** \"It's a B!\"\n\n**(0:13 - 0:18) - Letter C**\n*(Three curved pieces appear scattered)*\n**Voiceover:** \"These three curved pieces look tricky... *Slide!*\"\n*(Pieces snap perfectly into a ring and fuse into C)*\n**Voiceover:** \"They make a C!\"\n\n**(0:18 - 0:23) - Letter D**\n*(Two scattered pieces appear)*\n**Voiceover:** \"A straight line and a big curved piece. *Click!*\"\n*(Pieces slide and fuse into D)*\n**Voiceover:** \"We built a D!\"\n\n**(0:23 - 0:28) - Letter E**\n*(Four straight puzzle pieces appear scattered)*\n**Voiceover:** \"Four straight puzzle pieces. Let's stack them up! *Snap!*\"\n*(Pieces slide and fuse into E)*\n**Voiceover:** \"It's an E!\"\n\n**(0:28 - 0:33)**\n*(Outro screen appears)*\n**Voiceover:** \"You are a puzzle master! Great job!\""}
